##EDIT AND PREPARE CLIPS 
After downloading the source videos, the next task is to identify interesting moments and convert them into engaging short-form videos.
There are two approaches to finding interesting moments and two approaches to editing.


Finding interesting moments - 
Method 1: Manual identification
Open the downloaded source video.
Watch the video and look for engaging conversations, funny reactions, controversial opinions, educational information or storytelling.
Note down the timestamps of interesting moments.
Select moments that can work independently as short-form videos.
Extract the selected portions using your video editor.


Method 2: AI-assisted identification using Gemini
Copy the YouTube video URL.
Open Gemini.
Paste the YouTube link.
Ask Gemini to identify the most interesting and engaging moments.
Request timestamps for each suggested moment.
Review the suggested timestamps yourself.
Select the best moments for clipping.


Prompt - 
Analyze this YouTube video and identify the best moments for short-form content (Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts and TikTok).

Find moments that contain:

- Interesting conversations
- Funny or entertaining moments
- Controversial opinions
- Surprising statements
- Valuable information
- Strong emotional reactions
- Engaging storytelling

For each selected moment, provide:

1. Start timestamp
2. End timestamp
3. A brief description
4. Why the moment could engage viewers
5. A suggested opening hook

Prioritize moments that can work independently without requiring viewers to watch the entire original video.


Editing the clips - 
Method 1: Manual editing
CapCut – Beginner-friendly editing.
DaVinci Resolve – Advanced editing.
Adobe Premiere Pro – Professional editing.
VN Video Editor – Mobile editing.

Typical editing tasks:
Extract the selected portion.
Convert the footage into a 9:16 vertical format.
Adjust the framing and cropping.
Add animated captions and subtitles.
Highlight important keywords.
Add zoom effects and jump cuts.
Improve audio quality.
Add background music if permitted.
Export the final clip.


Method 2: Automated clipping tools
opusclip
vizard AI
Klap

Typical editing tasks ( done by the tool ): 
Detecting potentially engaging moments.
Extracting short clips from long videos.
Automatically generating captions.
Converting landscape videos into vertical videos.
Reframing speakers.
Adding templates and transitions.

Simply take the clips extracted from the source video, either manually or with the help of AI, and edit them. 
Make sure to follow all the editing specifications mentioned in the campaign's rules document.
